ask outcomes are satisfied with direct effective-permission tests and coherent final ACL state. The mandatory restart protocol covered node1: it captured a healthy pre-restart state, scheduled and observed the restart, demonstrated a changed boot identity, verified matching data and recovered permissions, and was independently corroborated by the lifecycle boot-identity snapshots.","limitations":["The restart acknowledgement was an executor-side confirmation that a delayed systemctl reboot had been scheduled, rather than a separate provider-control-plane acknowledgement; subsequent connection loss, low post-boot uptime, changed boot identities, and recovered state strongly corroborate that the restart occurred.","The final lifecycle collector did not itself probe /srv/reports; final and post-restart ACL behavior instead comes from executor commands captured shortly before that snapshot."]}
